The metacircular evaluator `META_CLOSED` (kamea-machine,
`crates/kamea-scheme/src/lib.rs`) compiled to the certified core, and
frozen — the `ArtifactN8` move applied to a program: derive with the
tool (here the Rust compiler), then pin the result as data and prove
about the pinned object. Nothing in the trust story depends on the
compiler; the theorems of later rungs are about `META` below.

**GENERATED — do not edit the term by hand.** Regenerate with

    BLESS_META_IMAGE=1 cargo test -p kamea-scheme --test meta_image

in kamea-machine, then copy `tests/golden/meta_image_lean.txt` (the
term) and `meta_image_tokens.txt` (the token string) here. The Rust
side of the pin is that same test un-blessed: the compiler's output
must equal the goldens. The Lean side of the pin is
`meta_image_pinned` below: a total printer for the shared difftest
token grammar (mirror of `kamea-diff`'s `enc_prog` and `KameaRef`'s
parser) evaluates on `META` to the identical token string, so both
systems hold the same term. (`meta_image_pinned` is proved by
`native_decide` — the compiled-evaluation axiom, standard in this
repo's witness files; the term itself and `toTokens` are plain
definitions usable without it.)

